; SIXTEEN BYTES MOVED DOWN 885 CELLS  leaving the source EMPTY; Entered where
; the source begins and it leaves the pointer on the source's last cell;
; Every move in it is relative  so the same text does the same job wherever it
; is included: it moves src through src plus 15 into src minus 885;
;
; THE SIBLING OF block/copy16  AND THE DIFFERENCE IS THE WHOLE POINT; that one
; stages each byte and hands it back  for an operand that is wanted again; this
; one does not  for an operand that is SPENT by the routine it feeds; A copy
; where a move belonged is not a slow move: it leaves the old value standing
; where the new one is about to be written  and in aes/cbcenc128 that meant
; the next chaining value was the sum of the ciphertext and the plaintext
; block that produced it; The first block was still right  because a block is
; emitted before it is chained  so only a message of TWO blocks or more could
; show it;
;
; IT ALSO TOUCHES NOTHING IT DOES NOT HAVE TO; block/copy16 stages 869 cells
; below its source  which in that mode is the cipher's own round key region;
; this routine has no stage  so those cells are never written at all;
; ASSERT ptr=+0
  [-L885+R885]
; the next byte
R1
  [-L885+R885]
; the next byte
R1
  [-L885+R885]
; the next byte
R1
  [-L885+R885]
; the next byte
R1
  [-L885+R885]
; the next byte
R1
  [-L885+R885]
; the next byte
R1
  [-L885+R885]
; the next byte
R1
  [-L885+R885]
; the next byte
R1
  [-L885+R885]
; the next byte
R1
  [-L885+R885]
; the next byte
R1
  [-L885+R885]
; the next byte
R1
  [-L885+R885]
; the next byte
R1
  [-L885+R885]
; the next byte
R1
  [-L885+R885]
; the next byte
R1
  [-L885+R885]
; the next byte
R1
  [-L885+R885]
; ASSERT ptr=+15
